Feature: Replacing and ending a plan
  The ground sends a new plan about once a second, with a new plan id each time. The plane
  flies the newest plan. If no new plan comes before the time to live ends, the plane circles
  where it is. Thus a plane that loses the ground does not fly away.

  Expectation: A new plan id replaces the plan
    The plane does not finish the old plan first. It turns to the new plan at once.

    Given the reported primitive is go to
    When the ground sends an orbit plan
    Then the reported plan goes up by 1
    And the reported primitive is orbit

  Expectation: A repeated plan id changes nothing
    The plane flies a plan id only once. If a plan comes again with the same id, the plane
    keeps the plan that it has, even if the new message has another primitive. Thus a plan
    that the link sends twice does not restart.

    The rule below is what the plane must do. It does not do it yet. The plane flies the first
    plan, but AG_PRIM shows the primitive of the new message (`prim=4`). Until this is
    repaired, do not use AG_PRIM to see what the plane flies after a repeated plan id.

    Given the reported primitive is go to
    When the ground sends the plan id again with an orbit
    Then the reply to the plan is accepted
    And the reported plan stays the same
    And the reported primitive is go to

  Expectation: A plan that runs out makes the plane circle
    If the time to live of the plan ends before a new plan comes, the plane circles where
    it is. It tells the ground why, with AG_FALL and the message "Agent: fallback 1". A short
    [[recovery]] can also show, as `recoveries` in the console. To give
    each plan more time, set `AGENT_GRACE`. It is in seconds, and it is 0 by default.

    Given the time to live of the plan is 5 s
    When the plane flies on for 10 seconds
    Then the reported fallback is plan expired

  Expectation: A new plan ends the circle
    The plane flies the new plan at once. With the parameters of `ardupilot/t1s.parm`, a short
    [[recovery]] can show in AG_FALL as 3 at the same time.

    Given the time to live of the plan is 5 s
    When the ground sends a go-to plan
    Then the reported fallback is none or recovery
